From 15b4d2cd5996a946671ff42faf053c90ce47b53b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mptfire <263163432+mptfire@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:17:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 02/22] web_fetch: a fetch owes the card, the prompt is the
 exfil gate

web_fetch never overrode mutates(), so it rode the read-tool path and
auto-ran in every mode including supervised, next to read_file and
grep. A fetched page is attacker-readable text; the same turn can read
a workspace secret, so injected instructions had a zero-prompt send of
that secret to any host the model named. The SSRF gate guards the
inbound direction only, and the checkpoint covers files, not outbound
bodies, so the card is the whole gate here.

Tools gain asks() (default: mutates()): the loop consults it beside
mutates(), web_fetch overrides it to true. Net: supervised,
accept_edits, and auto show a card with the URL before the dial;
full_access runs as before. README's only-network-traffic claim is
corrected to name fetch and search for what they are.
